{
 "id": "fox-approach-nair-dair",
 "name": "Read the stance",
 "part": "neutral",
 "characters": [
  "fox"
 ],
 "shield": "theirs",
 "goal": "Open up an opponent that stands, crouches or shields with the answer its stance allows",
 "why": "What an opponent is doing decides what opens it up. Standing, it takes the neutral air and the shine after it. Crouching, it takes the neutral air with no stun and hits back: a grab, or the down air, goes through. Shielding, it grabs after any gap: a grab beats the shield.",
 "switch": "every",
 "reset": {
  "after": "quiet",
  "seconds": 1
 },
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "Look at what the opponent is doing before Fox commits: standing, crouching or shielding. Then open it up: a neutral air into shine, a down air into shine, or a grab.",
  "expect": "Each try begins with Fox's jump, grab or shine and is judged when he has a grab, when his shine hits, or when the opponent hits or grabs him.",
  "example": [
   {
    "press": "Z",
    "frame": 1,
    "hold": 1
   }
  ],
  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: Z. The grab",
   "7": "Frame {f}: it has {opp}"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "Three stances",
    "text": [
     "Standing, {opp} is open: the neutral air hits, and the shine after the landing hits again.",
     "Crouching, it takes the neutral air with almost no stun and acts before Fox has landed. Shielding, it grabs the moment its shield stun is over."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         1,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 10,
        "hold": 6
       },
       {
        "press": "A",
        "frame": 16,
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         1,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 17,
        "hold": 13
       },
       {
        "press": "L",
        "frame": 28,
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": 37,
        "hold": 3
       },
       {
        "press": "B",
        "frame": 37,
        "hold": 2
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: X or Y tapped: a short hop",
       "10": "Frame {f}: the stick toward it: Fox drifts in",
       "16": "Frame {f}: A with the stick let go: the neutral air, late in the hop",
       "28": "Frame {f}: L, before the landing",
       "37": "Frame {f}: down-B on the first frame after the landing lag"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "What goes through",
    "text": [
     "A grab takes all three: it does not care about a crouch, and a shield does not stop it.",
     "Against a crouch the down air works too: its hits keep the opponent in stun until the shine. Against a shield an aerial that hits late in the fall, with the shine on the first free frame, is out before the grab."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "press": "Z",
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 1
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: Z. The grab",
       "7": "Frame {f}: it has {opp}"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  ]
 },
